[1.083165, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.714768, "o", "Initialized mnema project at ~/your-repository/.mnema\r\n  identity: mnid:4f215e7add40c7fd1615fbf401916cdc52ae54d5d0ce244b332e42dc28296fd9\r\n"]
[1.715021, "o", "  backup key: created and enrolled — private half at ~/.mnema/identity/backup/46ab9ed26155c2c7f29599850fda12571c4a0603f482fbe28ac1e46f21e01063.key\r\n  Move that file off this machine: a backup left on this disk is lost with it.\r\n\r\n"]
[1.715167, "o", "  mnema writes no file of yours. In Claude Code the mnema plugin hands this record to\r\n"]
[1.715224, "o", "  each session on its own. Without it, `mnema brief > MNEMA.md` puts what governs this\r\n  project in a file of its own — the `>` replaces the whole of the file it names — and\r\n  one line in a `CLAUDE.md` brings that file in (an `AGENTS.md` is read there only\r\n"]
[1.715244, "o", "  where no `CLAUDE.md` exists):\r\n"]
[1.715318, "o", "    @MNEMA.md\r\n"]
[1.715381, "o", "\r\n  Commit `.mnema/` with the repository: the record travels with it, and every clone reads it.\r\n"]
[1.715428, "o", "  Next: `mnema decision record <title> <rationale>`; `mnema status` shows where things stand.\r\n"]
[3.334753, "o", "\u001b[2m# write down a call, with the reasoning and what was turned down\u001b[0m\r\n"]
